---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party software
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

DATUM is distributed with libraries that carry their own licences. The MIT
licence above covers DATUM's own source only.

  Qt, via PySide6            LGPL-3.0
  OpenCASCADE, via
    cadquery-ocp             LGPL-2.1 with the OCCT exception
  VTK                        BSD 3-clause
    (not used by DATUM, but linked by OpenCASCADE's Python binding, so it
     has to be present for the kernel to load at all)
  NumPy                      BSD 3-clause
  cryptography               Apache-2.0 / BSD 3-clause
  Python                     PSF

In a built installation each of these stays a separate file under
_internal/, rather than being linked into DATUM itself, which is what lets
anybody replace one with their own build as the LGPL requires.
